  "created": "2026-08-14T13:35:44.493Z",
  "description": "Ships Rask.SQLite.Crdt's change feed to an object-storage bucket, so several devices sharing one SQLite database converge with nothing between them. Each device writes only under its own prefix, so no two clients ever write the same key and there is nothing to lock or retry; peers are found with a grouped listing and read forward from a per-peer watermark, so a sync costs what changed rather than what exists. Offline is the normal case: the database itself is the queue, so a failed sync loses nothing and losing the sync state costs only re-reading, never data.",
